<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swiss Federal Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swiss Federal Council is the seven-member executive of the Swiss Confederation, created by the federal constitution of 1848. Its members are elected by the Federal Assembly and govern collectively, each heading a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, with a president who rotates every year. Since 1959 the main parties have shared its seats by an informal 'magic formula'.</p></div>
